---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro';
import InnerHero from '@/components/InnerHero.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const title = 'Privacy Notice | Sana Patel Real Estate';
const description =
  'How Sana Patel Real Estate proposes to collect, use, disclose and protect information submitted through the SP_REBIRTH website.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath="/privacy/" noindex={true}>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />
  <InnerHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Clear about the information we ask for."
    lead="This pre-launch notice describes the SP_REBIRTH website data flows. It remains a release gate and must be checked against the final CRM, analytics, email, review and legal configuration before production."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <article class="container legal-copy">
      <p class="status-note">
        <strong>Pre-launch draft:</strong> do not remove the noindex directive until the final data destinations, retention
        rules, cookie/analytics approach, overseas-processing position and legal review are complete.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is collecting the information</h2>
      <p>
        This website is operated for {SITE.name}. Questions about information submitted through the website can be
        directed to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone.e164}`}
          >{SITE.phone.display}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit an enquiry, the website may collect your name, email address, phone number, property address or
        suburb, information about your current property-management situation, current property manager if you choose to
        provide it, preferred timing and your message.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website may also capture limited technical and attribution information associated with the enquiry, such as
        the page you arrived on, referral source and campaign parameters. The production system should collect only
        information reasonably necessary for the enquiry, website security and agreed measurement purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this information is collected</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiry information is intended to be used to respond to your request, understand the property or service you
        are asking about, arrange appropriate follow-up and understand which website or marketing activity generated
        genuine enquiries. Submitting an enquiry does not by itself subscribe you to unrelated marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>If you do not provide the information</h2>
      <p>
        You can browse the public website without submitting a lead form. If you choose not to provide the contact
        details or minimum property context required by a particular enquiry form, Sana Patel Real Estate may not be
        able to respond meaningfully to that request. You can instead contact Sana directly by phone or email.
      </p>

      <h2>Spam and security checks</h2>
      <p>
        Forms use Cloudflare Turnstile or an equivalent abuse-prevention control. Technical request information may be
        processed as part of this verification and for website security. The production configuration will document the
        security provider and relevant data-handling terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers and disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        The production website may use infrastructure, content-management, lead-delivery, email, analytics and
        review-display providers to operate the website and respond to enquiries. Personal information should only be
        disclosed to providers where reasonably necessary for those functions, or where otherwise authorised or
        required.
      </p>

      <h2>Overseas processing</h2>
      <p>
        Some cloud, content, email, analytics or security providers may process information outside Australia. The final
        production notice must identify whether overseas disclosure or processing is likely and, where practicable and
        legally required, the relevant countries or regions after the final vendor configuration is known.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, cookies and campaign measurement</h2>
      <p>
        The pre-launch site uses first-party browser session storage to retain the initial landing path, referrer path
        and explicit UTM campaign fields while a visitor moves between pages in the same browser session. Query strings
        and fragments are removed from stored landing/referrer URLs, and lead contact fields are not written to that
        session record. If browser storage is unavailable, the lead journey continues without persisted attribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party analytics will not be enabled merely because a tracking ID exists. The production implementation
        will document what is measured, which cookies or similar technologies are used, whether consent or another
        choice mechanism is appropriate, and how visitors can exercise any available choices.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        The final lead system must define an appropriate retention period and security controls for enquiry data.
        SP_REBIRTH will not intentionally keep website enquiry data indefinitely without a business or legal reason.
        Access should be limited to people and service providers who genuinely need it.
      </p>

      <h2>Access and correction</h2>
      <p>
        The final operating procedure will describe how an individual can ask what personal information is held about
        them and request correction where appropriate. Requests can begin through the contact details above.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy concerns or complaints</h2>
      <p>
        The final production policy will document how privacy concerns are received, investigated and responded to,
        including any external escalation information that applies to Sana Patel Real Estate.
      </p>

      <h2>Australian privacy requirements</h2>
      <p>
        Australian privacy obligations depend on the organisation and the circumstances. This website has been
        engineered with the Australian Privacy Principles and current OAIC collection-notice guidance in mind, but this
        draft does not state that every APP obligation applies to Sana Patel Real Estate. Applicability and final
        wording require legal/business review against the actual operating model.
      </p>

      <h2>Final review required</h2>
      <p>
        This page is an engineering draft, not legal advice. It must be reviewed and approved against the final CRM,
        email, analytics, Cloudflare, Sanity, Trustindex/review and data-retention configuration before production
        launch.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-copy {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }
  .legal-copy h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 2.8vw, 2.6rem);
  }
  .legal-copy p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .legal-copy a {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .status-note {
    padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--white);
    color: var(--ink) !important;
  }
</style>
